# Three database roles (docs/adr/0012, docs/operations/environments.md):
# - the owner of the tables runs the migrations, `npm run db:roles` and Prisma Studio;
MIGRATION_DATABASE_URL="postgresql://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/oliveira_erp"
# - the API's role, which row-level security applies to — `npm run db:roles`
#   creates it with the name and password written here;
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://oliveira_app:oliveira_app_dev@localhost:5432/oliveira_erp"
# - the BYPASSRLS role the seed (and later the demo reset) writes through.
ADMIN_DATABASE_URL="postgresql://oliveira_admin:oliveira_admin_dev@localhost:5432/oliveira_erp"

# Read by prisma/seed.ts. Bootstraps the first ADMIN account — left unset
# here on purpose (leave commented out to skip creating one; the seed is safe
# to re-run later once these are set).
# ADMIN_EMAIL="admin@example.com"
# ADMIN_PASSWORD="change-me"

# Also read by prisma/seed.ts. Defaults to system@oliveira.internal if unset —
# only needs overriding if that address collides with a real account.
# SYSTEM_ACCOUNT_EMAIL="system@oliveira.internal"
